      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I must reiterate, it's not recommended to self-medicate with a higher dose of Benadryl without consulting a doctor, especially if you're unsure of the severity of the reaction. Taking large doses of Benadryl without medical guidance can lead to serious side effects, such as drowsiness, dizziness, and potentially life-threatening anticholinergic toxicity. Additionally, some allergic reactions, including skin reactions, can worsen over time if left untreated.",
